# Timeline & version model

The user is learning this domain — keep names boring and comments short when a concept is interview-critical (split, overlap, three-way merge).

## Units & media
- Time: prefer **seconds** (number) for HTML5 video sync in v1; document if switching to frames
- MediaAsset: id, name, type, objectUrl (ephemeral — lost on refresh; intentional in early phases)
- Never version media bytes in v1 — version the timeline JSON that references assets

## Clips & tracks
- TimelineClip: id, assetId, trackId, timelineStart, trimStart, trimEnd
- Split = two clips, same assetId, adjusted trims — never duplicate media bytes
- Move = change timelineStart (and optionally trackId) only

## Versions & merge
- Version = named timeline snapshot + optional parentVersionId(s)
- Diff = clip ops: add | remove | trim | move | replace
- Conflict / Overlap = same trackId + overlapping time range changed on both sides since common base
- Merge: auto-merge non-overlaps; surface Overlaps in UI (Keep yours / Keep theirs / split)
- Do not silently last-write-wins the whole timeline
- Do not use CRDT auto-merge as a substitute for Overlap UX when combining Versions
